	"notes": "The UK government's homepage is one of the most disciplined layouts captured tonight: everything is capped at exactly 960 pixels wide, and that number does not change at all whether the screen is a laptop, a desktop, or a giant ultrawide monitor — the scan finds the identical 960 three times over. Inside that fixed column, the list of services on the left and the 'Featured' box on the right also use fixed pixel widths rather than a percentage split, so nothing about the page's content changes above 1280 pixels wide, only the quiet margin around it grows. Below that point everything stacks into one plain column, and the grid of 'Popular on GOV.UK' links goes from three columns down to one. A large cookie-consent banner also sits above the blue header in every one of these screenshots, which is worth knowing when comparing them.",
